---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base title="Eviction & Recovery of Possession Guidance" description="Step-by-step guidance through the legal eviction process under Act 220.">
  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap">
      <a href="/services/" style="color:#516784; text-decoration:none; margin-bottom:1rem; display:inline-block;">← Back to Services</a>

      <h1>Eviction & Recovery of Possession Guidance</h1>
      <p class="muted" style="max-width:680px; margin-bottom:2rem;">Step-by-step guidance through the complete legal eviction process under Act 220, from notice service to Rent Magistrate appearance to physical possession.</p>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#f0f4f8; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Why You Need This Service</h2>
        <p style="line-height:1.8;">Eviction in Ghana is a legal process with many steps. Get one step wrong and your eviction can be challenged, delayed, or rejected entirely. Common mistakes:</p>
        <ul style="line-height:1.8; margin:1.5rem 0;">
          <li>Serving notice incorrectly or without proof</li>
          <li>Not waiting the full notice period</li>
          <li>Filing with incomplete documents</li>
          <li>Not showing up to Rent Court hearing</li>
          <li>Not understanding what happens after magistrate's decision</li>
          <li>Trying to remove tenant illegally (locks, threats, disconnections)</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="line-height:1.8;"><strong>This guidance ensures you follow the legal path and avoid costly mistakes.</strong></p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#f9f9f9; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">What We Cover</h2>
        <ul style="line-height:1.8;">
          <li><strong>Legal Grounds:</strong> Are you allowed to evict, and on what grounds?</li>
          <li><strong>Notice Service:</strong> How to prepare and serve Form 9 correctly</li>
          <li><strong>Proof of Service:</strong> Documentation showing tenant was properly notified</li>
          <li><strong>Evidence Gathering:</strong> What to bring to Rent Court</li>
          <li><strong>Court Filing:</strong> When and how to file your application</li>
          <li><strong>Hearing Preparation:</strong> What to expect and how to present your case</li>
          <li><strong>Post-Judgment:</strong> What happens after magistrate's decision</li>
          <li><strong>Execution:</strong> How to legally remove tenant's possessions</li>
          <li><strong>Tenant Defenses:</strong> What arguments tenant might make and how to counter</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#f9f9f9; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">The Eviction Timeline</h2>
        <p style="line-height:1.8; font-weight:600; margin-bottom:1rem;">Typical eviction process under Act 220:</p>
        <ul style="line-height:1.8;">
          <li><strong>Week 1:</strong> Serve notice (Form 9) on tenant</li>
          <li><strong>Weeks 2–3:</strong> Wait for response (tenant may contest in 14 days)</li>
          <li><strong>Weeks 4–6:</strong> File at Rent Control office (if no payment/resolution)</li>
          <li><strong>Weeks 7–10:</strong> Attend Rent Court hearing(s)</li>
          <li><strong>Weeks 11–12:</strong> Magistrate issues decision</li>
          <li><strong>Weeks 13–16:</strong> Execution order and physical eviction</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="line-height:1.8; margin-top:1rem;"><strong>Total: 3–4 months from notice to possession.</strong> Our guidance helps you navigate each step correctly.</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#fff3cd; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">When You Need This Service</h2>
        <ul style="line-height:1.8;">
          <li>A tenant is refusing to pay rent and you want to evict</li>
          <li>You're about to serve notice and want to do it correctly</li>
          <li>You've already served notice and want guidance on next steps</li>
          <li>You're preparing for Rent Court hearing</li>
          <li>You want to understand your rights before attempting eviction</li>
        </ul>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#e8f4f8; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">The Risk of DIY Eviction</h2>
        <p style="line-height:1.8;">Many landlords try eviction without proper guidance and:</p>
        <ul style="line-height:1.8; margin:1rem 0;">
          <li>Get their eviction rejected by magistrate</li>
          <li>Serve notice improperly and have to start over</li>
          <li>Lose months of rent during the process</li>
          <li>Face counter-claims from tenant for illegal eviction</li>
          <li>Have to hire lawyer at higher cost to fix mistakes</li>
        </ul>
        <p style="line-height:1.8;"><strong>GHS 400 in guidance now prevents thousands in loss and stress.</strong></p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:2rem 0; padding:2rem; background:#f9f9f9; border-radius:8px;">
        <h2 style="margin-top:0;">Pricing & Turnaround</h2>
        <p style="font-size:1.2rem; font-weight:700; color:#516784; margin:0;">GHS 400</p>
        <p style="color:#666; margin:0.5rem 0;">Complete guidance from notice to resolution</p>
        <p style="font-weight:600; margin-top:1rem;">Turnaround: 2–3 working days</p>
      </div>

      <div style="margin:3rem 0; text-align:center;">
        <a href="/services/" style="display:inline-block; padding:1rem 2rem; background:#516784; color:white; text-decoration:none; border-radius:4px; font-weight:600; margin-right:1rem;">Request a Quote</a>
        <a href="https://wa.me/233208071633" style="display:inline-block; padding:1rem 2rem; background:#f0f4f8; color:#516784; text-decoration:none; border-radius:4px; font-weight:600; border:1px solid #516784;">Chat on WhatsApp</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
